-- title:
--   Dedekind: f'(α) multiplies the codifferent into the integers
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\Omega =$ `PadicAlgCl p` be the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_p$ used in the project, equipped with its norm. Let $F$ be an intermediate field of $\Omega/\mathbb{Q}_p$ that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_p$, and let $E$ be an intermediate field of $\Omega/F$ that is finite-dimensional over $F$. Let $\alpha \in E$ satisfy $\|\alpha\| \le 1$ for the norm of its image in $\Omega$, and assume that $\alpha$ generates $E$ over $F$, in the sense that the intermediate field generated by $F$ and $\{\alpha\}$ inside $E$ is all of $E$. Let $z \in E$ be such that for every $w \in E$ with $\|w\| \le 1$ (norm computed in $\Omega$) the trace $\operatorname{Tr}_{E/F}(zw) \in F$ satisfies $\|\operatorname{Tr}_{E/F}(zw)\| \le 1$ in $\Omega$; that is, $z$ lies in the codifferent of $E/F$. Then the element $z \cdot f'(\alpha) \in E$, where $f = \operatorname{minpoly}_F(\alpha)$ and $f'(\alpha)$ is the value at $\alpha$ of the derivative of $f$, has norm at most $1$ in $\Omega$.
--
--   This is Dedekind's theorem that $f'(\alpha)$ lies in the different of $E/F$ for any generator $\alpha$ of $E$ over $F$ integral over the valuation ring, stated for finite extensions inside a fixed algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_p$ and in terms of absolute values rather than ideals. It is used in the construction of elements of bounded norm in trace duals, via [`PadicAlgCl.exists_forall_traceDual_norm_le_rpow_sup_cyclotomicTower`](thm.html#PadicAlgCl.exists_forall_traceDual_norm_le_rpow_sup_cyclotomicTower).
